Wait — about `execGetWatermark()` on mount: it reads from the PM view state. In the dialog, calling it during render is a side effect in render — better in useEffect. But useState initializer runs once. Calling execGetWatermark() in the initializer is fine-ish (it reads state, no side effects), but it's a store read during render of a component that mounts on dialog open. Since the dialog only mounts when opened, the initializer read is a one-time read — acceptable. But to be cleaner and avoid re-render issues, useEffect + setState. Actually simplest: read in useState initializer — it's a pure read of the store, no subscription. That's fine and avoids a flash of defaults.

